# Project Scope & Reference

## v0.1 Scope (do not overbuild)

Deliver:
- `plan` — generate CommitPlan from hunks using LLM structured output
- `apply` — apply CommitPlan deterministically using `git apply --cached` + `git commit`
- `init` — write default `.engine.yaml` config

Defer: PR planning, risk scoring, release tooling, indexes, daemons, GUIs.

## Canonical Types & Interfaces

Use these names consistently; do not rename or reinvent.

Domain types (`engine/models/`):
- `Hunk` — { HunkID, FilePath, Header, Patch, Summary }
- `CommitPlan` — { ToolVersion, BaseRef, Style, Commits }
- `CommitUnit` — { ID, Type, Scope, Subject, Body, Breaking, Footers, Hunks }
- `CommitStyle` — { Convention, MaxSubjectLen, AllowedTypes, Scopes }

Context (`engine/context/`):
- `EngineContext` — { BaseRef, Hunks, RecentCommits, Config }

Interfaces:
- `Plan` — { Validate() error }
- `Planner` — { Name() string; BuildPlan(ctx EngineContext) (Plan, error) }
- `Executor` — { Execute(plan Plan) error }
- `ReasoningEngine` — { CallStructured(schema JSONSchema, input any) (any, error) }

## Folder Structure (target layout)

```
/cmd            — root.go, plan.go, apply.go, init.go
/engine
  /context      — repo_context.go, diff_parser.go, hunk_hasher.go
  /models       — hunk.go, commit_plan.go, change_intent.go
  /reasoning    — client.go, structured_call.go, retry.go
    /schemas
  /planners     — planner.go, commit_planner.go, commit_schema.go
  /validators   — commit_validator.go
  /executors    — executor.go, git_executor.go
/config         — config.go
```

## Deliverables for each change

- Update types and interfaces cleanly
- Add or update tests
- Provide brief notes in PR-style summary (what/why)
